### Limitations the authors admit
- 2025ApJ...984L..15P: Classification is subjective and inclination-biased
- 2025ApJ...984L..15P: Vertically isothermal assumption is a major limitation
- 2023MNRAS.526L..41P: Cloud contamination hides the channels where a velocity kink is expected, so no robust kinematic mass is possible.
- 2020ApJ...898...10T: Model CBD larger than observed; magnetic field not included; high-velocity blueshifted components near Source N not reproduced; infall not identified observationally
- 2014ApJ...796....1T: Missing flux and outflow complicate other lines near systemic velocity; temperatures in hydrodynamics (isothermal 13.5 K) and radiative transfer (power law) are inconsistent.
- 2024A&A...691A..57M: Parameter space degenerate; no ALMA simulator applied; pulsations missing
- 2015ApJ...798..124R: Data cannot distinguish between gap and double power-law forms; dust opacity degenerate with surface density
- 2024A&A...682A..56Z: Disk model lacks the east-west asymmetry of the observed source, so outskirts are overpredicted
- 2012Natur.490..232M: Intensity contrast between spiral windings and interwinding material indicates a more complicated mass-loss-rate variation than modelled
- 2020A&A...633A..13D: Model not formally fit; chosen by eye
- 2020A&A...633A..13D: Mass-loss rate is a lower limit as optical depth is about unity
- 2016PASJ...68...43K: Estimates depend on beta (dust particle size) and dust filtration model
- 2024MNRAS.534.2904C: Residuals are model dependent; Keplerian background assumed
- 2020ApJ...888L...4T: Instant accretion at the sink radius may overestimate planet accretion
- 2019A&A...622A..75L: Degeneracy among simulation parameters cannot be quantified; fit by eye
- 2019A&A...622A..75L: Planet not confirmed; high-contrast searches needed
- 2025ApJ...986L..11S: Low S/N; EDDY ignores beam convolution; visibility mass inconsistent with Teff
- 2025ApJ...986L..11S: Substructure tentative; BIC prefers no ring
- 2023PASJ...75.1105K: Temperature in the radiative transfer is inconsistent with the locally isothermal hydrodynamics; the inner boundary may cause artifacts; the tail feature may come from the unresolved circumplanetary …
- 2023PASJ...75.1105K: Inclination damping is not included
- 2017ApJ...851L..23C: Gaps only partially resolved, degeneracy between width and depth
- 2017ApJ...851L..23C: Other explanations (MHD, instabilities) remain possible
- 2024ApJ...976..132H: FUV fields are upper bounds from projected separations; temperature uncertainty dominates dust-trap and planet-mass estimates; SVI is approximate
- 2020MNRAS.499.3837G: Only seven orbits tested; comparison is visual and subjective
- 2018ApJ...869L..47Z: Gap profiles fitted at fixed 1000 orbits; dust feedback ignored
- 2018ApJ...869L..47Z: Occurrence rates are upper limits since gaps may not be planetary
- 2024A&A...688A.102T: Models do not fully reproduce SPHERE morphology; comparison is qualitative, deferred to future work
- 2020MNRAS.499.3857N: Kozai-Lidov oscillations were not seen in hydrodynamic simulations; N-body neglects gas effects
- 2017ApJ...839L..24M: Aim is morphological similarity, not exact fit; different uv coverage used
- 2025ApJ...984L..21B: Single simulation snapshots with particular parameters; no Hall effect or ambipolar diffusion; no embedded planets; limited 20-100 au range
- 2020ApJ...895L..18B: Mutual inclinations cannot be determined from dust alone due to unknown orbital direction; gas model has no uncertainties for the gap.
- 2019A&A...625A.118K: Hydro models assume vertically isothermal disk; delta v_rot may be underestimated
- 2019A&A...625A.118K: Beam smearing and limited spectral resolution complicate rotation-curve interpretation
- 2021A&A...654A..35B: Simulations cannot reproduce the spiral break, gap and ring
- 2018ApJ...869...17L: Formal errors on fit parameters likely underestimated
- 2018ApJ...869...17L: Dust mass uncertainties ignore temperature and optical depth
- 2018ApJ...869...17L: Model fails to reproduce amplitude of azimuthal asymmetries
- 2018MNRAS.475.5296D: Fit done by eye; degeneracy cannot be quantified
- 2019AJ....158...15P: Not an exhaustive fit; no dust growth, fragmentation or back-reaction
- 2016ApJ...820L..25Y: Column density biased by poorly constrained dust and gas temperature profiles.
- 2018ApJ...857...87L: Degeneracy among acceptable alpha values not fully characterized
- 2019ApJ...871..107F: Model does not fully reproduce observations because of 2D temperature structure uncertainties
- 2019ApJ...871..107F: Insufficient sensitivity to see the co-rotation bump
- 2018ApJ...866L...6C: Innermost gap poorly resolved; shape unconstrained
- 2016ApJ...819..134B: 2D only; scattered light compared only qualitatively
- 2019ApJ...879L...2M: Model 12CO shows a central peak far stronger than observed, likely from the inner boundary
- 2019ApJ...880...69Y: Spiral velocities depend on the assumed mid-plane location and conserved angular momentum
- 2019ApJ...880...69Y: Inner-radius line width overestimated, so column density, Tex and tau at the inner radius may be underestimated
- 2019AJ....157..237R: Models are generic, not fine tuned; viscosity, scale height and gas surface density not varied; inner cavity not modeled
- 2016ApJ...829L..35T: Results depend on assumed smooth temperature profiles; more bands needed
- 2016ApJ...829L..35T: Planet mass is an upper limit
- 2019A&A...624A..33V: Unclear whether mm excess is spiral counterpart or vortex; higher resolution needed
- 2016A&A...586A..99H: Cannot infer both surface density and opacity from single wavelength; errors are formal only
- 2016ApJ...818..158A: Only 17 of 780 baselines exceed 10 km; images could be improved
- 2018A&A...619A.161C: Emission only marginally optically thin so masses are lower limits; large uncertainties in opacity and gas surface density
- 2018A&A...619A.161C: Spectral index decrease may be due to optical thickness rather than grain growth
- 2019NatAs...3..278K: Gas and dust mass estimates have large systematic uncertainties from optical depth, temperature and H2/CO.
- 2018ApJ...857...18S: Inner and outer gap depths not well constrained; planet mass estimates are crude without gas information
- 2017ApJ...846...70P: Two of the spectral indices are only lower limits
- 2016PhRvL.117y1101I: Large CO optical depth prevents ruling out a shallow gas gap in the inner gap
- 2017A&A...607A..55V: Dust temperature is likely overestimated so dust mass is a lower limit
- 2018MNRAS.474.5105B: Data not flux calibrated

