  - software: phantom
  - parameter: alpha_av = 0.2; inner radius 5 au; H/R=0.1 at 50 au; gamma=0.8; accretion radius 0.125 Hill radius [Modeling: "we set the shock viscosity to $\alpha_{\rm av} = 0.2$"]
  - assumption: Vertically isothermal; self-gravity neglected; disk mass 5e-3 Msun [Modeling: "We neglect self-gravity and use a disk mass of $5 \times 10^{-3} \, \mathrm{M}_\odot$ for all disks"]
  - validation: phantom+mcfost benchmarked by Bae et al. [Modeling: "The combination of phantom and mcfost was benchmarked and validated by (cite: Bae_exoALMA)."]
- step 4: Radiative transfer synthetic CO channel maps
  - method: mcfost for dust temperature and CO maps with Voronoi cells matched to SPH particles; Tgas=Tdust, LTE [Modeling: "We postprocessed the models with the radiative transfer code mcfost (cite: Pinte2006; Pinte2009) to compute the dust temperature structure and CO maps"]
  - software: mcfost, pymcfost
  - parameter: 12CO abundance 1e-4 relative to H in warm layer; depleted below 20 K by a variable factor [Modeling: "Below 20 K, we deplete this abundance by a factor that we allow to vary"]
  - assumption: Astrosilicate grains, dn ∝ a^-3.5 da, 0.03-1000 micron, gas-to-dust 100; zero turbulent velocity; 1 Myr isochrones [Modeling: "a uniform gas-to-dust ratio of 100"]
  - validation: Visual comparison of kink shape and amplitude with data [Comparison with Data: "The planet model matches the observations well for LkCa 15, J1615, and J1842, in terms of both shape and amplitude of the kink."]
- limitation (authors): Classification is subjective and inclination-biased [A Variety of Kinematic Substructures: "Our classification is subjective, and some sources clearly exhibit multiple types of substructures."]
- limitation (authors): Vertically isothermal assumption is a major limitation [Discussion: "One major limitation of our models is the assumption of a vertically isothermal profile in phantom."]
- not stated (card): Weighting schemes (robust, taper) and exact channel binning for each disk's reimaged cubes; Which channels are shown for each disk; Exact dynamite fitting setup and uncertainties; Criteria for the visual classification; Beam and noise for the Figure 6 cubes; Planet-wake projection details; Specific depletion factor grid values; Number of mcfost photons and grid setup

