  - parameter: Grid 1024x768, disk 10-500 au, dust grain size 0.15 mm, h=0.05(r/r0)^0.25 [2.1 Hydrodynamic simulation: "The disk extends from 10 to 500 au, and is simulated with a resolution of $1024\times768$ grids along the radial and azimuthal direction."]
  - assumption: Isothermal T(r)=24.1(r/r0)^-0.5; viscosity nu=alpha c_s h [2.1 Hydrodynamic simulation: "we assume the turbulent viscosity has the form $\nu = \alpha c_{\textrm{s}} h$"]
  - fitting: Manual exploration of more than 100 simulations compared with I16 fiducial surface densities; no MCMC [3 Results: "We have performed more than one hundred simulations in total with various initial conditions of planet mass, disk mass and effective viscosity."]
