- result: Nominal planet masses at 59, 105, 160 au = 0.46, 0.46, 0.58 ± not stated M_J [abstract: "three half-Jovian-mass planets (0.46, 0.46 and 0.58 $M_\textrm{J}$) at 59, 105 and 160 au"]
- result: Nominal alpha_in and alpha_out = 1e-5 and 7.5e-3 ± not stated dimensionless [3.2 Varying alpha: "we choose $\alpha_\textrm{in} = 10^{-5}$ and $\alpha_\textrm{out} = 7.5 \times 10^{-3}$"]
- limitation (authors): Degeneracy among acceptable alpha values not fully characterized [4.2: "our simulations also show there is some degeneracy of acceptable $\alpha$ values, which is not fully characterized in this study."]
- not stated (card): Public ALMA data processing/imaging details (beam, rms, calibration) not given; taken from I16; LA-COMPASS code version and dust-gas coupling/boundary condition details; CO abundance and isotope ratios, and the radially varying CO/H2 profile; RADMC-3D photon numbers and beam convolution parameters; Quantitative goodness-of-fit metric; fits judged by eye

### 2019ApJ...871..107F: Gas Density Perturbations Induced by One or More Forming Planets in the AS 209 Protoplanetary Disk as Seen with ALMA (2019; protoplanetary_disks, astrochemistry; observational_alma_primary)
